title: The Economic Crisis
new-page: true
is-card: true
view-if: crisis_urgency >= 1 and crisis_program_timer = 0 and economic_plan = 0 and black_thursday_seen == 1
frequency: 200
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; crisis_program_timer = 5
card-image: img/bankrun.jpg
tags: party_affairs, govt_affairs

= Addressing the Economic Crisis

Comrades! The Great Depression is the final epoch of this treacherous era. Though the failures of Sparatakus haunt us, as does the suffering of our brothers in Italy- which has fallen to the fascist meance. 

One comfort, still, have we, that this depression that has emerged here is clearly the final and terminal crisis, or a symptom of it! The global economy is collapsing! Unemployment is surging, about a third of the German work force is unemployed and the government hides it via invisible unemployment! Those labouring in very few hours or who have given up. 

Meanwhile our industrial production has fallen by about 42%, the heavy industry meanwhile is down at 70%. This is largely a capital problem! Because guess what? Only 36% of our factories are operating at total capacity! The financiers, the Anglo Saxon bankers, all are behind this.

? if spd_relations += 50 right_strength += 40 ? That being said, how we react to this crisis is not really about the economics it's more so about is the working class on the defence of the attack? After all, perhaps it would make more sense to launch a defensive struggle alongside the SPD for the German workers. ? 



