From study, RGO, which was a trade union formed in late 1929 and held its first congress in 1929 ot oppose the SPD Unions, leader Paul Merker got kicked out in April of 1930 for "linke Abweichungen" (left deviation) because he wanted a less sectarian approach(?). 
Interestingly, this hardline is very unpopular because in Dec 1929 the KPD had 135k members and 120k by Spring of 1930. 
Though after Merker is fired they soften their rhetoric, einheitsfront von unten but also flirt with national demagogy over Young Plan.

Interestingly  the KPD declared Germany Fascist in December of 1930 and cites Bruning which is disavowed by the Comintern in January of 1931 who then say SPD are the main enemy of the "maturing fascist republic" just before the Prussian landtag referendum.
Comintern influence will play a role here presumably the KPD can say "no germany is fascist" and not merely a maturing republic.]




- @support_centrist: Support the Centrist view.
- @support_labor: Support the Labor view.
- @support_left: Support the Left view.
- @support_moderate: Support the Reformist view.
- @defer: Defer making a decision until we have more information.

@support_centrist
subtitle: Let the depression play itself out.
on-arrival: center_strength += 5; center_dissent -= 5; conciliator_dissent += 10; wtb_support -= 1; left_dissent += 10;

Woytinsky and the trade unions vehemently criticize the centrists for their policy. The workers are starving; are we going to callously abandon them and side with bourgeois austerity? On the other hand, the centrists criticize Woytinsky for promising the workers false hope; their position is that nothing can be done to alleviate the depression. They also speak of the fear of another round of hyperinflation that may result from deficit spending.

Our policy course is currently that nothing can be done to alleviate the depression.


@support_labor
subtitle: Call for increased public works and fiscal stimulus.
unavailable-subtitle: The Labor faction is not strong enough.
choose-if: historical_mode == 0 or (conciliator_strength >= left_strength and conciliator_strength >= center_strength and conciliator_strength >= right_strength)
on-arrival: center_dissent += 10; left_dissent += 5; conciliator_strength += 5; wtb_support += 1;
go-to: plan_adopted if wtb_support >= 3; plan_support if wtb_support < 3

@plan_support

Our support of the WTB plan alienates the orthodox Marxists of the Centrist faction, and faces both opposition and support from a variety of sources across the spectrum. Leftists argue that the plan is flawed because it leaves capitalism intact, while some reformists are cautiously optimistic.

We have not yet convinced the party to formally adopt the plan. More work needs to be done.

@plan_adopted
on-arrival: wtb_adopted = 1; conciliator_dissent -= 15; right_dissent -= 10; conciliator_strength += 10; center_strength -= 10; center_dissent += 20; left_dissent += 5; economic_plan = 1

With our hard work, we have finally convinced the majority of the party to adopt the WTB plan! [? if spd_in_government == 1 : We can begin implementing the plan as soon as possible, as long as we have the Economic or Finance ministries. ?][? if spd_in_government = 0 : We should emphasize the plan in our electoral propaganda. ?]

@support_left
subtitle: Call for mass nationalizations and the transformation of the economy.
unavailable-subtitle: The Left faction is not strong enough.
choose-if: historical_mode == 0 or (left_strength >= conciliator_strength and left_strength >= center_strength and left_strength >= right_strength)
on-arrival: left_strength += 10; right_dissent += 5; conciliator_dissent += 5; nationalization_support += 2
go-to: support_left_progress if nationalization_support < 3; adopt_left if nationalization_support >= 3

@support_left_progress

We attempt to convince the party to support a program of mass nationalizations in response to the economic crisis. Leftists argue that this policy is in accordance with our long-standing socialist platform, while reformists and some trade unionists argue that the plan is unrealistic, and that we need to focus on more immediate improvements to workers' lives.

We have not yet formally adopted the plan. More work needs to be done.

@adopt_left
on-arrival: left_strength += 15; left_dissent -= 10; right_dissent += 10; neorevisionist_dissent += 8; conciliator_dissent += 6; nationalization_adopted = 1; coup_progress += 1; economic_plan = 3; spd_relation += 5*(1-dissent)

With our hard work, we have convinced the majority of the party to adopt the socialist economic plan! [? if spd_in_government == 1 : We can begin implementing the plan as soon as possible, as long as we have the Economic or Finance ministries. ?] Bourgeois opposition is likely to be fierce. [? if spd_in_government == 0 : It might be difficult to enact the plan, given present conditions. ?]

@support_moderate
subtitle: Call for a limited program of job creation without deficit spending.
unavailable-subtitle: The Reformist faction is not strong enough.
choose-if: historical_mode == 0 or (right_strength >= left_strength and right_strength >= center_strength and right_strength >= conciliator_strength)
on-arrival: moderate_plan_support += 1; right_strength += 8; right_dissent -= 5; left_dissent += 6; conciliator_dissent += 5
go-to: adopt_moderate if moderate_plan_support >= 2; support_moderate_progress if moderate_plan_support < 2

@support_moderate_progress

We attempt to convince the party to support a moderate program of job creation without deficit spending. Advocates of the moderate plan argue that this plan is most likely to receive support from the bourgeois parties, and most practical in the immediate term. Opponents in the left and labor factions criticize the plan for being inadequate in its ambition.

We have not yet adopted the plan. More work needs to be done.

@adopt_moderate
on-arrival: right_strength += 10; right_dissent -= 10; left_dissent += 8; conciliator_dissent += 6; moderate_plan_adopted = 1; economic_plan = 2; coalition_dissent -= 1 if unemployed > 15; z_relation += 5;

With our hard work, we have convinced the majority of the party to adopt the moderate job creation plan! [? if spd_in_government == 1 : We can begin implementing the plan as soon as possible, as long as we have the Economic or Finance ministries. ?]

@defer

We hold off on making a decision on economic policy, awaiting more information. Woytinsky and his supporters argue that inaction is a form of action of its own. 
